'''yieldable''' (yēl′da-bl), ''a.'' [< ''yield'' + ''-able''.] That may or can be yielded.—'''2.''' That may can yield; inclined to yield; complying.

'''yieldableness†''' (yēl′da-bl-nes), ''n.'' A dispo tion to yield, comply, or give in.
